WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.140
we have a voicemail number that you can call
anytime of day.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:10.420
That number is two one nine two David P. here's
a really good practical question about getting

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.670
engaged in politics.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:12.960
Take a listen to this.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:13.960
Hi David.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:14.960
My name is Carlos.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.560
I've been trying to call it on the show for
awhile and haven't been successful.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.560
So I thought I'd maybe a message.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
And here's the question.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:26.289
I know the big topic right now is impeachment,
some pressing issues, but one of the things

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:33.110
that I wanted to see you cover, I wanted to
hear your opinion on is how you think that,

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:40.020
um, the people who are somewhat less than
wealthy can enter politics successfully.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:44.330
I've been interested in politics for many
years and I'm getting to a point in my career,

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:50.530
I'm kind of considering retiring and going
into politics, but yeah, not exactly Andrew

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.580
Yang or Tom [inaudible] or somebody else who
already has a whole bunch of them.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:55.580
Right?

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:56.580
Oh, okay.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.580
Somehow they got cut off.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:58.580
I guess he was going to say a whole bunch
of money.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.990
So here's the thing, this is a great question
to be asking.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:05.680
Uh, what w we actually, we need more people
that don't come from the same three or four

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.860
industries in politics.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.130
But you're right, if you are not in a financial
position that is a particularly strong, it's

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.940
going to be very difficult to become, for
example, a Senator.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.930
Uh, it potentially, there are places as we
know, people like AOC who without a lot of

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.790
money have become, uh, elected members of
the house of representatives.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:24.110
But that is also difficult.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:27.390
The best thing to do is to get involved at
the local level.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.050
And this accomplishes a lot of things.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:34.040
Number one, to get on school boards, even
sometimes to run for city council.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.830
I've seen people with no money get on city
councils in different places.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:42.570
It doesn't take a lot of money to do it and
it's a great place to start, but it also does

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.619
something else that the left has been failing
out.

00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:49.979
I've been talking for years to anyone who
will listen about how the left has been failing

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:55.290
at getting the bullpen built up, getting the
farm league built up.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:02:00.590
Uh, and one of the best ways to do that is
by starting to get into the city councils

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.470
and the school boards and all of the other
things you can influence policy.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:10.200
Yes, on a local level, but in ways that do
matter to the people in that community doesn't

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:15.420
require the out-sized resources that are often
required to run for higher office.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:19.320
And it can be used if your aspiration is eventually
higher office.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:25.810
It can be used as a precursor to start building
a following, building a coalition.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.310
So that's what I would encourage you to do.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.000
I have no idea where you live and what's available
in terms of government, but there are lots

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.840
of options you can get on the board of local,
non-commercial radio or television stations.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.010
That's something I did back in North Hampton,
Massachusetts.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:43.090
I wasn't on the board of NCTV North Hampton
community television now, uh, relaunched as

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.670
North Hampton, open media.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:47.880
Uh, there are limitless options that require
very little money.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.470
Some require no money whatsoever because these
positions are just open sometimes and you

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.910
can use them to get to other positions if
that's what you want.

00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.430
So that would be my advice.

